# docs/ is default-deny, matching the codegate client.
#
# Listing what may be committed is the only version of this rule that holds:
# a denylist of plan/checklist/handoff names needs somebody to have thought of
# the name first, and two planning documents had to be purged from this
# history precisely because nobody had. docs/ is for architectural
# documentation — how the thing works, for someone reading the code. Anything
# describing how it got built goes stale the day it is written and does not
# belong in a published repository.
#
# To add a document, un-ignore it here, deliberately.
/docs/**
!/docs/
!/docs/testing.md

# Planning artefacts, wherever somebody puts them.
*hackathon*
*-handoff.md
*-tasks.md
*-checklist.md
*-plan.md
PLAN.md
PLANS.md
TASKS.md
TODO.md
ROADMAP.md
NOTES.md
SCRATCH.md
tests/e2e/.auth/

# Written by semantic-release so the container job knows what was cut.
.release-version
